{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"55320d54f5be6d52","name":"card_event_bomber_run_brit","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/WinterWar/events/card_event_bomber_run_brit","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"BOMBER RUN","text":"Deal 2 damage to target unit. Deal 5 instead if you control a bomber with 5+ attack.","flavorText":"Operation Hydra, carried out by RAF Bomber Command on the night of August 17th 1943, targeted a German research center in Peenemünde. Group Captain John Searby led the operation; it was Bomber Command's first use of a master bomber to direct the attack. This mission marked the beginning of the Crossbow campaign against the German V-weapon program. Even though it resulted in the loss of 215 crew members and 40 bombers for the British, and casualties among enslaved workers in a nearby forced labor camp, it also inflicted damage on the Luftwaffe, causing delays in V-2 rocket testing and production. However, its overall effectiveness in slowing down German V-weapon production has been debated as the Germans had already dispersed V-2 manufacturing to other locations by 1942.","faction":"Britain","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_bomber_run_brit","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_bomber_run_brit_title","SourceString":"BOMBER RUN","LocalizedString":"BOMBER RUN"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_bomber_run_brit_text","SourceString":"Deal 2 damage to target unit. Deal 5 instead if you control a bomber with 5+ attack.","LocalizedString":"Deal 2 damage to target unit. Deal 5 instead if you control a bomber with 5+ attack."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_bomber_run_brit_history","SourceString":"Operation Hydra, carried out by RAF Bomber Command on the night of August 17th 1943, targeted 